    "help": {
      "exit_code": 0,
      "stdout": "Source files -> flat graph facts (JSONL on stdout, or --sqlite)\n\nUsage: ryii [OPTIONS] [PATH]...\n       ryii <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  capabilities  Declared language and tooling capabilities\n  fast          Syntax-only whole-project facts (no compiler)\n  slow          The SCIP oracle written as fast's tables\n  scip          Raw SCIP index rows\n  graph         Ask one question of the resolved call/type graph\n  cleave        Move one item into another file, with its imports\n  move          Move a file and repair every specifier that names it\n  rename        Rename a symbol and every occurrence bound to it\n  query         Run a tree-sitter query over files\n  region        Replace a generated region between sprefa markers\n  watch         Stream fact deltas as the worktree changes\n  diff          Fact delta between two commits\n  ingest        Validate and re-emit foreign TSI JSONL\n  schema        Print the output record schema\n  trail         Print the last N runs from the trail\n  stratify      Rank files from entrypoints and propose dependency-first numeric prefixes\n\nArguments:\n  [PATH]...  Files, directories, or globs; - reads a path list from stdin\n\nOptions:\n      --fast-receivers <written>  Resolve written receiver types in fast mode\n      --pattern <GLOB>            Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input; repeatable\n      --entry <FILE>              Run on the files FILE reaches over imports (universe: the PATH inputs, else FILE's project)\n      --depth <N>                 Import hops from --entry\n      --root <DIR>                Corpus root\n      --kinds <KINDS>             Fact kinds per file (cst,type,call,df,data,cfg)\n      --arms <ARMS>               Resolve arms under --resolve (call,type,flow)\n      --sqlite <PATH>             Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout\n      --bench                     Time extraction and print per-family counts to stderr\n      --resolve                   Resolve cross-file edges over all given paths\n      --scip-index <FILE>         Load this index.scip\n      --rust-checker              Use rust-analyzer for Rust call/type targets\n      --ts-checker                Use the TypeScript compiler for TS call/type targets\n      --go-checker                Use go/types for Go call/type targets\n      --scip-build                Build the index with the language's indexer, then load it\n      --scip-timeout <SECS>       Seconds allowed for one indexer run under --scip-build\n      --scip-deps                 File-to-file edges folded from a SCIP index\n      --deps                      File-to-file edges resolved from syntax, no index\n      --package-deps              Manifest-to-manifest workspace edges\n      --file-fact                 Prepend one file record: path, digest, bytes, lines\n      --lines                     Add 1-based line/col beside every span\n      --witness                   Wrap output in the TSI envelope\n      --max-bytes <BYTES>         Skip inputs over this many bytes (0 = no limit)\n  -h, --help                      Print help\n  -V, --version                   Print version\n\nLogging: RUST_LOG (default sprefa_extract=info,hafley_scm=info), HAFLEY_LOG_FORMAT=json|text\nCapabilities: `ryii capabilities` prints the declared language matrix.\nSQLite with --resolve stores phase 1 per-file and phase 2 project rows; stdout streams phase 2 only. Every SQLite unresolved row has its path.\nBuild: git hash: 2c93c0a3d2d7, datetime: 2026-10-06T20:24:08Z\nDeclared language capabilities:\nLANGUAGE     PLANES                 RESOLVE  REHOME                 RENAME  CHECKER         SCIP\nrust         cst,types,call,df      call+types manifests,plan_check   yes     rust-analyzer   rust\ngo           cst,types,call,df      call+types                        no      go-types        go\nkotlin       cst,types,call,df      call+types                        yes     -               kotlin/java\nmarkdown     cst,types              +types                          no      -               -\nprolog       cst,types,call,df      call                            yes     -               -\npython       cst,types,call,df      call+types                        no      -               python\ndata         cst,data                                               no      -               -\nts           cst,types,call,df      call+types manifests,text_spellings,plan_check yes     tsgo            typescript\ngdscript     cst                                                    no      -               -\ncommonlisp   cst                                                    no      -               -\ntypespec     cst                                                    no      -               -\nfallback     cst,call               call                            no      -               -\ncpp                                                                 no      -               cpp\n",
      "stderr": ""
    },
